      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to view traces",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 66
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Distributed Tracing\n\nTraces are exported from the application via **OpenTelemetry OTLP** (`micrometer-tracing-bridge-otel` + `opentelemetry-exporter-otlp`) to **Tempo**.\n\n- Selected Tempo datasource: **${DS_TEMPO}**\n- Pivot to traces in **Explore -> ${DS_TEMPO}** and search by service `carddemo`, or paste a `traceId`.\n- Logs carry the `traceId`/`spanId`/`correlationId` (structured Logback), so a log line can be correlated to its trace.\n- Sampling probability is 1.0 in the local profile, so every request/job is traced locally.\n"
      },
      "datasource": null
    }
